---
const withBase = (path: string) => `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}${path.replace(/^\//, '')}`;
const points = [
  { n: '1', title: 'Kitchen sink and branch drain', detail: 'Water from the kitchen sink enters a smaller branch drain. Grease, food scraps and soap residue can restrict this section before it joins the larger building drain.', clue: 'The kitchen sink is slow or backs up while other fixtures may still drain.', href: '/services/kitchen-bathroom-drains/' },
  { n: '2', title: 'Bathroom fixtures and branch drains', detail: 'Bathroom sinks, tubs and showers connect to branch piping that carries wastewater toward the main building drain. A blockage in one branch may affect only those fixtures.', clue: 'A bathroom sink, tub or shower drains slowly or backs up.', href: '/services/kitchen-bathroom-drains/' },
  { n: '3', title: 'Toilet connection and main building drain', detail: 'Toilet waste joins the building drain. When a restriction is farther downstream, flushing a toilet can make another low fixture gurgle or back up.', clue: 'A toilet flush affects a tub, shower or floor drain.', href: '/services/main-drain-cleaning/' },
  { n: '4', title: 'Basement floor drain and laundry branch', detail: 'A floor drain is often one of the lowest openings in a basement. A washer discharge or a downstream restriction can cause wastewater to appear there.', clue: 'Water rises through the floor drain when the washer runs or other fixtures are used.', href: '/services/basement-floor-drains/' },
  { n: '5', title: 'Main building drain and cleanout', detail: 'The building drain collects wastewater from the fixture branches and carries it toward the foundation exit. A cleanout, where present and accessible, provides a point to access the line.', clue: 'Several fixtures are affected together or wastewater comes up at a low drain.', href: '/services/main-drain-cleaning/' },
  { n: '6', title: 'Building sewer to the public sewer', detail: 'The buried building sewer carries wastewater from the house to the public sewer connection. Roots, buildup, separated joints or damaged pipe can cause recurring trouble along this run.', clue: 'The main line keeps clogging or multiple fixtures back up repeatedly.', href: '/services/sewer-line-cleaning/' }
];
---
<section class="where-drains-fail py-16 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="where-drains-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#f36b21]">How wastewater leaves the house</p>
    <h2 id="where-drains-heading" class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">From the kitchen sink to the main sewer</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">A kitchen sink has its own branch drain. That branch joins the home's larger drainage piping, which carries wastewater out through the building sewer to the public sewer. Select a numbered point to see what that part does and what a blockage may look like.</p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_.85fr] lg:items-start">
      <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-[#eef3f8] p-3 shadow-sm sm:p-6">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 900 570" role="img" aria-labelledby="drain-map-title drain-map-desc" class="block h-auto w-full">
          <title id="drain-map-title">House drainage diagram from kitchen sink to public sewer</title>
          <desc id="drain-map-desc">Cutaway schematic showing kitchen sink, bathroom fixtures, toilet, laundry and basement floor drain connecting through branch drains to a main building drain, foundation exit, buried building sewer and public sewer. A vent stack rises through the roof.</desc>
          <defs>
            <pattern id="drain-soil" width="14" height="14" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M0 14L14 0" stroke="#d5dce2" stroke-width="1"/></pattern>
          </defs>
          <path d="M18 390H882V548H18Z" fill="url(#drain-soil)"/>
          <path d="M18 390H882" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="3"/>
          <path d="M65 390V145L270 35L475 145V390Z" fill="#fff" stroke="#26343a" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M48 149L270 24L492 149" fill="none" stroke="#e9682b" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M270 38V170" stroke="#2385a2" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <path d="M258 38H282" stroke="#2385a2" stroke-width="6"/>
          <text x="292" y="58" fill="#17627b" font-size="15" font-weight="800">VENT STACK</text>
          <path d="M270 170V345H520V420H815" fill="none" stroke="#26343a" stroke-width="16" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M270 170V345H520V420H815" fill="none" stroke="#80c7df" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M145 210V300H270" fill="none" stroke="#26343a" stroke-width="10" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M145 210V300H270" fill="none" stroke="#80c7df" stroke-width="4"/>
          <path d="M145 210V198H176V210" fill="none" stroke="#26343a" stroke-width="4"/>
          <path d="M355 195V305H270" fill="none" stroke="#26343a" stroke-width="10" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M355 195V305H270" fill="none" stroke="#80c7df" stroke-width="4"/>
          <path d="M410 195V275H270" fill="none" stroke="#26343a" stroke-width="10" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M410 195V275H270" fill="none" stroke="#80c7df" stroke-width="4"/>
          <path d="M190 325V345H270" fill="none" stroke="#26343a" stroke-width="10" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M190 325V345H270" fill="none" stroke="#80c7df" stroke-width="4"/>
          <path d="M455 330V345H520" fill="none" stroke="#26343a" stroke-width="10" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M455 330V345H520" fill="none" stroke="#80c7df" stroke-width="4"/>
          <path d="M520 420V345" stroke="#26343a" stroke-width="10"/>
          <path d="M508 345H532" stroke="#26343a" stroke-width="5"/>
          <path d="M815 420V465M780 465H850M780 482H850M780 499H850" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <path d="M520 390V420" stroke="#e9682b" stroke-width="5" stroke-dasharray="6 5"/>
          <text x="270" y="15" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e293b" font-size="16" font-weight="800">HOUSE DRAINAGE</text>
          <text x="150" y="185" fill="#1e293b" font-size="14" font-weight="700">KITCHEN SINK</text>
          <text x="350" y="175" fill="#1e293b" font-size="14" font-weight="700">BATHROOM</text>
          <text x="410" y="255" fill="#1e293b" font-size="13" font-weight="700">TOILET</text>
          <text x="110" y="322" fill="#1e293b" font-size="13" font-weight="700">LAUNDRY</text>
          <text x="390" y="325" fill="#1e293b" font-size="13" font-weight="700">FLOOR DRAIN</text>
          <text x="350" y="375" fill="#1e293b" font-size="13" font-weight="800">MAIN BUILDING DRAIN</text>
          <text x="555" y="405" fill="#1e293b" font-size="13" font-weight="800">CLEANOUT</text>
          <text x="650" y="445" fill="#1e293b" font-size="13" font-weight="800">BUILDING SEWER</text>
          <text x="815" y="530" text-anchor="middle" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="800">PUBLIC SEWER</text>
          <g class="map-hotspot"><a href="#drain-point-1" aria-label="Point 1, kitchen sink and branch drain"><circle cx="145" cy="225" r="18"/><text x="145" y="231">1</text></a></g>
          <g class="map-hotspot"><a href="#drain-point-2" aria-label="Point 2, bathroom branch drains"><circle cx="355" cy="215" r="18"/><text x="355" y="221">2</text></a></g>
          <g class="map-hotspot"><a href="#drain-point-3" aria-label="Point 3, toilet connection"><circle cx="410" cy="285" r="18"/><text x="410" y="291">3</text></a></g>
          <g class="map-hotspot"><a href="#drain-point-4" aria-label="Point 4, laundry and basement floor drain"><circle cx="455" cy="345" r="18"/><text x="455" y="351">4</text></a></g>
          <g class="map-hotspot"><a href="#drain-point-5" aria-label="Point 5, main building drain and cleanout"><circle cx="520" cy="345" r="18"/><text x="520" y="351">5</text></a></g>
          <g class="map-hotspot"><a href="#drain-point-6" aria-label="Point 6, buried building sewer"><circle cx="680" cy="420" r="18"/><text x="680" y="426">6</text></a></g>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="px-2 pb-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Schematic, not to scale. Actual fixture locations, venting, pipe routes and sewer connections vary by house. The drawing explains the general flow path; it is not a plan of a specific property.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-1">
        {points.map((point) => <a id={`drain-point-${point.n}`} href={withBase(point.href)} class="drain-failure-card group rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm transition hover:border-[#303437] hover:shadow-md focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-[#303437]"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="map-number">{point.n}</span><div><h3 class="text-lg font-black leading-snug text-slate-950 group-hover:text-[#303437]">{point.title}</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">{point.detail}</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm font-bold text-[#303437]">What you may notice: {point.clue}</p><span class="mt-2 inline-block text-sm font-black text-[#f36b21] underline underline-offset-4">See related A-1 service →</span></div></div></a>)}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">These are possible trouble areas, not a diagnosis. The fixture pattern, pipe access and inspection findings determine the next step.</p>
  </div>
  <style>
    .map-hotspot a{cursor:pointer}.map-hotspot circle{fill:#e9682b;stroke:#fff;stroke-width:4;transition:fill .15s ease}.map-hotspot text{fill:#fff;font-size:15px;font-weight:900;text-anchor:middle;pointer-events:none}.map-hotspot a:hover circle,.map-hotspot a:focus circle{fill:#26343a;stroke:#fbbf24;stroke-width:5}.map-hotspot a:focus{outline:none}.map-number{display:inline-flex;width:2rem;height:2rem;flex:0 0 2rem;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border-radius:9999px;background:#26343a;color:#fff;font-weight:900}.drain-failure-card:target{border-color:#e9682b;box-shadow:0 0 0 2px rgb(233 104 43 / 18%)}
    @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.map-hotspot circle{transition:none}}
  </style>
</section>